# Part 1 – Dark Mode Toggle

## What I Learned

Dark mode allows users to switch between light and dark themes.

Instead of changing every element individually with JavaScript, we simply add or remove a CSS class.

Example:

```javascript
document.body.classList.toggle("dark-mode");
```

When the button is clicked, JavaScript adds or removes the `dark-mode` class from the `<body>` element.

CSS then changes the appearance automatically.

