# Part 2 – Local Storage

## What I Learned

Normally, refreshing a webpage resets everything.

Local Storage allows browsers to remember information even after the page is refreshed.

Save data:

```javascript
localStorage.setItem("theme", "dark");
```

Retrieve data:

```javascript
localStorage.getItem("theme");
```

Remove data:

```javascript
localStorage.removeItem("theme");
```

This allows the portfolio to remember the user's preferred theme.

