# Part 3 – Scroll To Top Button

## What I Learned

A floating button appears after scrolling down the page.

JavaScript listens for scrolling:

```javascript
window.addEventListener("scroll", () => {});
```

If the user scrolls more than 300 pixels:

```javascript
scrollBtn.style.display = "block";
```

Otherwise:

```javascript
scrollBtn.style.display = "none";
```

Clicking the button smoothly returns the page to the top.

```javascript
window.scrollTo({
    top: 0,
    behavior: "smooth"
});
```

